# Debug console history — ↑ brings the last submission back into the
# input, ↓ past the newest restores what was typed. Verifies the
# history walk without a live adapter. Re-aimed (debug-ui): the REPL
# pane's row selection went with it; the console is a scrollback.

# Plain-text fixture on purpose: a .rs file in a Cargo-less temp
# workspace makes rust-analyzer fail discovery, and its stacked
# error toasts paint OVER the console input row — the "> y"
# assertion then fails on any machine with rust-analyzer installed
# (found 2026-08-25 after months of environment-dependent red).
write notes.txt "hello\n"
open notes.txt
command dap.repl
expect pane "Debug"
type "x"
key enter
type "y"
expect screen contains "> y"
key up
expect screen contains "> x"
key down
expect screen contains "> y"
type "z"
expect screen contains "> yz"
